#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# region_intersection

#% text
# `region_intersection(r1, r2, ...)` is the intersection of plane polygons as a polygon (`empty_region(2)` when they do not meet).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
region_intersection(rectangle([0, 0], [2, 2]), triangle([[1, 1], [3, 1], [1, 3]]))
#% output
#= polygon([[1, 1], [2, 1], [2, 2], [1, 2]])

#% text
# A circle and a disk with exact data meet in the arc of the circle inside the disk:

#% cell
region_intersection(disk([0, 0], 1), circle([0, 1], 1))
#% output
#= circle([0, 1], 1, [(7/6)*pi, (11/6)*pi])

